    "result_text": "The full build succeeds with all tests green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI added a city-capacity rule that rejects owner creation with **409** when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners.\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (and mirroring the existing `EnsureUniqueOwnerHousehold` pattern), I added:\n\n- **`EnsureCityHasCapacity`** \u2014 a small, single-purpose function that counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed) and throws when the count is \u2265 50.\n- **`CityAtCapacityException`** \u2014 a checked exception so it surfaces on the `throws` clause and routes to an escalation handler.\n- **`CityAtCapacityExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds 409 with a `ProblemDetail`, identical in shape to the household handler.\n- **Escalation YAML** mapping the exception to its handler.\n- One line of wiring in `owners.POST.yml`: a new `ensureCityCapacity` step inserted after the household check.\n\nStructural impact was kept low: each new behaviour is its own cohesive class with near-zero surrounding complexity (WMC_other), and the only *edited* function is none \u2014 I only inserted a new step into an existing YAML and added new files, so no existing method's complexity was grown.",
